dsqt provides CMake targets:

    find_package(Dsqt CONFIG REQUIRED)
    target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE Dsqt::Dsqt)

Or link individual modules:

    find_package(Dsqt CONFIG REQUIRED COMPONENTS Core Bridge Waffles Touch)
    target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE Dsqt::Core Dsqt::Bridge)

Spout is available as a separate component:

    find_package(Dsqt CONFIG REQUIRED COMPONENTS Spout)
    target_link_libraries(main PRIVATE Dsqt::Spout)

The QML modules are added to QML_IMPORT_PATH automatically; DSQT_QML_DIR
holds their location if you need it for qt_add_qml_module or deployment.

Windows executables that use TouchEngine should call:

    dsqt_deploy_runtime_dlls(main)

Note: dsqt is compiled against the Qt kit named by your triplet's
DSQT_QT_VERSION. Building with a different Qt kit means selecting a
different triplet.

To choose modules explicitly, disable default features in the application manifest:

    { "name": "dsqt", "default-features": false, "features": ["qsys"] }

Core is always included. Optional features are bridge, waffles, qsys, spout,
touch and touchengine. The default feature set preserves the full package.
Waffles does not require Bridge; add bridge for CMS content integration.
Request only the same components in find_package(Dsqt COMPONENTS ...).
ProjectCloner writes these selections and the package version pin for you.
Core in this preview requires Qt 6.12, even when Waffles is disabled.
